# CODEOWNERS — the ownership half of the selective code-owner review gate
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# The standard: musher-dev/platform ADR 0134, checked by engineering-conventions
# COMM-09 (no `*` catch-all) and COMM-10 (every anchored path exists). The
# other half is a ruleset with `require_code_owner_review: true`, applied
# from musher-dev/infra-github.
#
# How review works here:
#
#   A pull request that touches NO path listed below merges on green CI alone:
#   the required checks are the gate. That includes dependency bumps to
#   package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml, which CI verifies, not a reviewer.
#   A pull request that touches a listed path also needs its owner's approval.
#   GitHub waives that on the owner's own pull requests.
#
# What is owned, and why:
#   /.github/   the gate and the release path: this file, the CI workflows,
#               the release workflow that publishes @musher-dev/musher-sdk to
#               npm with build provenance, and the release-please config
#   /.npmrc     where the @musher-dev scope resolves; a change here can point
#               installs of our own packages at another registry
#
# Everything else is unowned on purpose. Listing a path is a commitment to
# review every change to it, so keep the list short.
#
# Syntax rules that bite:
#   - NEVER add a `*` catch-all (COMM-09). It makes every pull request
#     codeowned and brings back blanket review of the whole repository.
#   - LAST matching pattern wins — order from broad to specific.
#   - ALL owners for a pattern go on ONE line.
#   - Owners need EXPLICIT write access to this repo, or the entry is silently
#     ignored and the path becomes unowned. GitHub lists such lines at
#     `gh api repos/musher-dev/typescript-sdk/codeowners/errors`.
#   - A root-anchored path must exist (COMM-10): after a rename, the old line
#     protects nothing.

/.github/    @musher-dev/sdk
/.npmrc      @musher-dev/sdk
